      "itemDescription": "<p>Eli Lilly, the Indiana-based pharma company, is celebrating its 150th anniversary in grand style: Its revenues have tripled since 2018, to $65.2 billion last year. It owes its surge to Mounjaro (for diabetes) and Zepbound (for weight management), which together command about 60% of the manically growing U.S. market for GLP-1 drugs.</p>",
