      "itemDescription": "<p>Founded over 145 years ago in Indianapolis, pharmaceutical company Eli Lilly established its first European affiliate in 1934. Lilly has provided more than two million doses of diabetes and cancer medicines to hospitals and patients in Ukraine via humanitarian partners, and its Foundation aims to extend Lilly's reach and impact and support programs that align with its philanthropic priorities. The pharma company's Skills First approach gives individuals without four-year degrees access to job opportunities that may not be available through traditional recruiting practices; apprentices receive a combination of formal training, on-the-job learning and mentoring in a key functional area to equip them for a full-time role.</p>",
